  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In September 2025 testimony, David A. LaCerte said artificial intelligence, data centers, and reindustrialization compound issues requiring planning, forecasting, and regulatory oversight from states and FERC. In February 2026 testimony as Commissioner, he described the AI race as transforming how Americans engage, transact, and compete, called the power grid a major battlefield, and said FERC should lead reforms to ensure data centers and chip manufacturing get needed energy on time. He also said China has been adding electric capacity rapidly while the U.S. faces interconnection bottlenecks, and that failing to meet the moment could jeopardize national security and America’s global competitive advantage.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s2",
    "s4",
    "s3",
    "s5"
   ],
   "sentences": [
